-- Q230: C Corporations [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Section 311, when a corporation distributes appreciated property, it recognizes gain as if the property were sold at FMV. Nexus recognizes $30,000 gain on Park's distribution ($80,000 FMV minus $50,000 basis). However, Section 311(a) prohibits loss recognition on distributions of depreciated property, so Nexus cannot deduct the $15,000 loss on Lee's vehicle. Distribution amounts are measured at FMV.
Wrong (B): Distribution amounts are measured at FMV, not adjusted basis, because FMV represents the economic benefit received by the shareholder.
